  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "A triangular array of \\(2016\\) coins has \\(1\\) coin in the first row, \\(2\\) coins in the second row, \\(3\\) coins in the third row, and so on up to \\(N\\) coins in the \\(N\\)th row. What is the sum of the digits of \\(N?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\)",
    "B": "\\(7\\)",
    "C": "\\(8\\)",
    "D": "\\(9\\)",
    "E": "\\(10\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The total number of coins is\n\\[\nS=1+2+\\cdots+N.\n\\]\nWrite a second copy of this sum in reverse order. Pairing corresponding terms gives \\(1+N\\), \\(2+(N-1)\\), and so on. There are \\(N\\) pairs, each totaling \\(N+1\\), so\n\\[\n2S=N(N+1).\n\\]\nSince \\(S=2016\\), we need\n\\[\nN(N+1)=4032.\n\\]\nThe consecutive integers \\(63\\) and \\(64\\) have this product:\n\\[\n63\\cdot64=4032.\n\\]\nThus \\(N=63\\). Adding another row always increases the total number of coins, so no other positive row count works. The requested digit sum is \\(6+3=9\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
